"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Potato","ingredient/potato"]]}]},"dish/imqaret":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/imqaret","n":"Imqaret","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Maltese cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Imqaret are traditional Maltese sweets made with pastry and a filling of dates. The word imqaret in Maltese, is the plural of maqrut (diamond-shaped) and it signifies the diamond shape of the sweets – even though in many cases they are sold in a rectangular shape. They are very popular in Malta and they are sold in street markets, as well as in village feasts, in some cases served with ice-cream."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-imqaret"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Imqaret"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Maltese cuisine","cuisine/maltese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"More from Maltese cuisine","links":[["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Maltese bread","dish/maltese-bread"],["Pastizz","dish/pastizz"]]}]},"dish/katt-bafla":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/katt-bafla","n":"Katt bafla","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Rajasthani cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Katt bafla is a popular and traditional dish from the Kota and Bundi districts of Hadoti region in Rajasthan, India. It is a famous dish across the north Indian states in India. Traditionally this dish is made on every occasion in Rajasthan. Bafla is a type of spherical wheat bread whereas the katt is a type of barfi made with a mixture of unsalted wheat bread coarse powder with ghee and jaggery powder. Traditionally this dish is served with daal and kadhi."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-katt-bafla"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Katt_bafla"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Rajasthani cuisine","cuisine/rajasthani-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":3,"links":[["Ghee","ingredient/ghee"],["Jaggery","ingredient/jaggery"],["Whea